import ../../../ui/overlays.dl

class:
    patterns:
        overlay test state
    members:
        order as an integer
        consumed as a boolean

to get [read overlay test input] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set state to context as a pointer to overlay test state
    set state's order to state's order * 10 + view's input code
    return state's consumed

to [paint overlay test] {a pointer:context} [on] {UI frame:frame}:
    set state to context as a pointer to overlay test state
    set state's order to state's order * 10 + frame's view's input code

to [close overlay test] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set state to context as a pointer to overlay test state
    set state's order to state's order * 10 + view's input code

set view to a new UI view
set context to a new overlay test state
set input to (the function named "read overlay test input $ in $") as a pointer
set paint to (the function named "paint overlay test $ on $") as a pointer
set closing to (the function named "close overlay test $ in $") as a pointer
set first to a UI overlay in (the address of view) with context ((the address of context) as a pointer) handling input input painting paint closing closing
set second to a UI overlay in (the address of view) with context ((the address of context) as a pointer) handling input input painting paint closing closing
set view's input code to 3
ignore process UI overlays in (the address of view)
require condition (context's order = 33) reporting "Input did not visit both overlays."
set context's order to 0
set context's consumed to true
require condition (process UI overlays in (the address of view)) reporting "An overlay could not capture input."
require condition (context's order = 3) reporting "Consumed overlay input reached a lower layer."
set context's order to 0
draw UI overlays on (@intrinsic("construct", UI frame, the address of view, true))
require condition (context's order = 33) reporting "Painting omitted an overlay."
detach UI overlay second in (the address of view)
require condition (view's overlays = first) reporting "Detaching the top overlay removed the remaining layer."
set context's order to 0
close UI overlays in (the address of view)
require condition ((context's order = 3) and (view's overlays = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI overlay))) reporting "Closing a view leaked its overlay or skipped its notification."
print line "UI overlays share input capture, painting and lifetime across drivers."
